B.a14=new A.bV("rd_mcq_6","Which five physical parameters are evaluated as part of the Silverman\u2013Andersen Score (SAS)?",B.aaB,1,"The Silverman\u2013Andersen Score evaluates 5 parameters, each scored from 0 to 2 (total 0\u201310): Upper chest movement (synchronized, lag, or see-saw), lower chest retractions, xiphoid retractions, nares dilatation, and expiratory grunt. An SAS \u22643 indicates mild RD, while \u22654 indicates moderate-to-severe RD.","Silverman\u2013Andersen Score",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Respiratory Distress in Neonates" (August 2026), SILVERMAN\u2013ANDERSEN SCORE; MCQs RD.docx Section 1 Q6')
B.adl=s(["All term neonates presenting with transient tachypnea","Preterm infants <34 weeks gestation requiring respiratory support","Only preterm infants who fail CPAP and require mechanical ventilation","All preterm neonates <34 weeks"],t.s)
B.a1g=new A.bV("rd_mcq_7","According to the STW algorithm, which group of neonates should receive caffeine citrate therapy as part of their initial management?",B.adl,1,"Caffeine citrate is indicated for all preterm infants <34 weeks gestational age who require respiratory support (such as CPAP or oxygen) as per protocol.","Caffeine",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Respiratory Distress in Neonates" (August 2026), START CPAP; MCQs RD.docx Section 1 Q7')
